    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Jack is a roof tiler. He is offered a job of laying $205\\text{ m}^2$ for \\$3198. Jack wants a rate of $\\frac{\\$18}{\\text{m}^2}$. Should he take the job or not?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. The offered rate is $\\frac{\\$15.60}{\\text{m}^2}$, below $\\frac{\\$18}{\\text{m}^2}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Offered rate}&=\\frac{\\$3198}{205\\text{ m}^2}\\\\&=\\$15.60/\\text{m}^2\\end{align*}$$\nJack should not take the job because the offered rate is below his required rate of $\\frac{\\$18}{\\text{m}^2}$.",
